{"event_type":"review","id":"744f1501c366c74654a45a018b5bf4054d4a5ccb5db407d4588aa11bb2d0bd32","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T03:08:12Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/01cdd0fa321ef11d56c20206cfbd8972bb476ec3051186fffe6cd7b9a44db109","sha256":"01cdd0fa321ef11d56c20206cfbd8972bb476ec3051186fffe6cd7b9a44db109"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/7548ed6fa16ed2be90766d6346515dee7d9e66eac0f49a446cfefade9e82c855","sha256":"7548ed6fa16ed2be90766d6346515dee7d9e66eac0f49a446cfefade9e82c855"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/07825aea4687895ccdf05920ad8eba674131a6d2322f1a8ad22237fd86d348b8","sha256":"07825aea4687895ccdf05920ad8eba674131a6d2322f1a8ad22237fd86d348b8"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/bc1ecd37a514b71514211e48e83325a09e66ab3a314bcb3840001fc69d64394d","sha256":"bc1ecd37a514b71514211e48e83325a09e66ab3a314bcb3840001fc69d64394d"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/2f36a459a57b593c6107113f7930f411270de183404a2ae5940a5e7aa4f05f7f","sha256":"2f36a459a57b593c6107113f7930f411270de183404a2ae5940a5e7aa4f05f7f"}],"attempt_id":"c40929dd9046d4cc434ba6098b7c93f331cbafa852f54f9d1dbccdbdac6ae6d5:0:1","base":"82efadcd2a4b2801057add5b9f321e7a75ab60ac","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"9854017285f297af74d291730dc3b2558967d314","body":"**Rejected usage bypasses the unpriced-usage trip under `capUsd`.**\n\n`observeResult` discards the whole `usage` object when `isValidUsage` fails. A usage object with a non-integer count or an extra key becomes `undefined`. `hasRealUsage` is then `false`, so the unpriced trip does not run. When a USD cap is configured, the run can continue past the cap with no trip. The `src/kernel/**` path rule requires that unpriced usage under a configured `maxUsd` trips loud.\n\nThe same discard happens on both caller paths:\n- `src/kernel/runner.ts:1466-1467` passes `validSpendEvidence(worker)` to `observeResult`.\n- `src/kernel/runner.ts:1561-1566` passes `validSpendEvidence(evidence)` to `observeResult`.\n\nThe two guards also disagree. `workerResultOfValue` checks only that each count is finite and non-negative. It does not require integers. A worker result with a fractional count passes that guard, and `validSpendEvidence` then removes its usage.\n\nThe contract in `src/kernel/types.ts:390-392` states that such folds \"fail loud, never fail open.\" The guard's comment says a lying measurement is treated as zero evidence. That intent conflicts with the fail-loud rule for measurements that still carry tokens.\n\nA possible remedy is to have `validSpendEvidence` report that usage was present but rejected. `observeResult` would then trip under `capUsd` for that case. An absent usage object should not trip. The NaN and negative cases need a deliberate decision, because the current design treats them as zero evidence. The remedy spans `observeResult`, `validSpendEvidence`, and the runner's two call sites, so no localized diff is given.","id":"d4623e35e52622c53449e722197339647eb6b329aad72f9c57ba9b322d7aca3f","intervals":[],"path":"src/kernel/governor.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Rejected usage bypasses the unpriced-usage trip under `capUsd`."}],"head":"1596857b4e69dc30c933a99e8451e7f251aad466","head_tree":"a619b07177492e5c80d4ce45880731ec409f8b2c","input_scope":[{"blob":"1c0762f53764fa12b5737be94273c79513d24366","intervals":[[30,33],[44,44],[59,60],[67,68],[116,116],[118,133],[153,158],[177,203],[205,516],[520,523],[525,534],[562,567],[588,588],[590,594],[618,619],[621,623]],"path":"src/kernel/README.md"},{"blob":"9854017285f297af74d291730dc3b2558967d314","intervals":[[3,3],[5,14],[18,18],[21,22],[36,36],[38,38],[40,41],[45,46],[73,167],[245,252],[265,265],[26